 "final_message": "All 12 work items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the 2 new ones). I didn't add tests for the other fixes, so I haven't run them.\n\n- **Items 1\u20133:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate` and `conversions_in_window` now follow sections 1\u20133.\n- **Items 4\u20135:** `parse_session_log` now maps the `converted` values `1`, `0` and empty to True, False and None, and skips blank, whitespace-only and `#` lines. Bad field counts or non-integer days raise `ValueError` with `line N`, counting skipped lines.\n- **Items 6\u20138:** `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow sections 5\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added one test for `None` counting as not converted and one for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, the `conversions_in_window` entry now says the last `days` entries, and there is a new `daily_conversion_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** I found and fixed three more deviations in the rest of the package:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and sorts its keys.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` now resets the run at a day with no flagged sessions. It also counts only days above 0.\n\nSPEC doesn't say what to do with a `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made that raise `ValueError` with `line N` too. Say if you'd rather it be handled differently.",
